[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"211","stub":{"id":"211","section":"Tarbell Pocket to Yucca Creek","altname":"","river":"Kaweah, North Fork","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112878","location":{"latitude":"36.6080017089844","longitude":"-118.913497924805"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"118157","location":{"latitude":"36.5444984436035","longitude":"-118.895202636719"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"211","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Paul Raffaeli testified:\n\nA group of us paddled most of the run mentioned in your online description.\n\nThe section we ran I briefly described below.. we put in perhaps 1/2 to 1 mile above the \"Put -In\" slide described and pictured here [http://www.ptone.com/Kayak/UNFK/index.html](http://www.ptone.com/Kayak/UNFK/index.html \"http://www.ptone.com/Kayak/UNFK/index.html\")\n\nCertainly from where we put-in this is not a class5+ run\n\nAt the flow we ran this (1.4 on NF Gage)  I would rate it mostly class 4++ / 5-\n\n\\\\*\\\\*\\\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nThis was the first time down for all of us in this group and here is a very brief summary.\n\n(The NF Gage was 1.4)\n\nOn Sunday we decided to do the Upper North Fork of the Kaweah... a 5 mile carry in (thanks salamander kayak-pak) and 5 or so miles down a lot of big but manageable rapids, it was a great adventure because of the big hike-in from the Yucca Creek trailhead (I ran across a very healthy looking Black Bear when I was hiking ahead by myself), the big drops and slides, and the fact that none of us knew the run or even exactly how long it was. It was a great but long 5 miles with lots of scounting, some portaging, some minor rescues, some mank, but mostly all very good fun...we finally got to the take-out 1/2 hour before dark..pretty exahausted, packed up and coffee'd home the almost 4hr drive.\n\nOur crew for the weekend was BillTut, BrianK, Nate, Brendan, and I.","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"6.6","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112878","118157"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-118.91374039252906,36.60872267650933],[-118.91399959252868,36.60870360984268],[-118.91422839252829,36.60873407650928],[-118.91448052586122,36.608726476509275],[-118.914663525861,36.608669276509374],[-118.91482359252741,36.60855860984287],[-118.9149533925272,36.608425076509775],[-118.91502952586042,36.608238209843364],[-118.91506019252701,36.608051276510366],[-118.91506019252701,36.607811009844056],[-118.91506032586034,36.60774607651081],[-118.91500679252708,36.60763547651101],[-118.91499912586046,36.607574476511104],[-118.91499919252709,36.6074600098446],[-118.91506012586034,36.607326476511446],[-118.91514392586022,36.60722740984494],[-118.91534999252656,36.60712820984515],[-118.91551032585964,36.60702520984529],[-118.91558672585955,36.60684967651224],[-118.91560959252617,36.60671620984573],[-118.91563979252612,36.60652920984603],[-118.91570879252602,36.60643380984618],[-118.91580019252586,36.60634607651298],[-118.91598339252556,36.606262209846484],[-118.91629612585844,36.60618207651328],[-118.91638772585827,36.60615540984662],[-118.91654792585804,36.60603327651347],[-118.91664719252458,36.60592647651367],[-118.91667752585785,36.60580827651381],[-118.9166697925245,36.60573967651396],[-118.91660879252458,36.60565947651406],[-118.91644859252487,36.60549547651431],[-118.91612839252537,36.60524760984805],[-118.91601392585888,36.60513687651485],[-118.91592979252567,36.60497287651515],[-118.91585352585912,36.60457607651574],[-118.91587652585905,36.60409160984983],[-118.91